{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:0.4", "PA_ja_220:1.1"], "en": "10. The Dhammadhajajātaka “You live happily indeed,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:1.2"], "en": "having come from the kingdom to the forest.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:1.3"], "en": "“Thus you sit alone at the foot of a tree,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:1.4"], "en": "meditating like a beggar.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:2.1"], "en": "“I am one whose mode of life is happiness;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:2.2"], "en": "Having come from the kingdom to the forest,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:2.3"], "en": "I sit alone at the foot of a tree,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:2.4"], "en": "meditating like a pauper.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:2.5"], "en": "\"Recalling the Dhamma of the virtuous.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:3.1"], "en": "The *Dhammadhajajātaka*, the tenth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:3.2"], "en": "The seventh chapter, the *Bīraṇathambhavagga*.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:4.1"], "en": "Its summary verse:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:5.1"], "en": "Then the excellent Bīraṇathambha, the Naṭa,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:5.2"], "en": "Bharu the king, and the supreme Puṇṇanadī.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_220:5.3", "PA_ja_220:5.4"], "en": "The mouse that speaks much about fire and wind was bitten by a beggar while standing on a branch of the sahala tree.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
]
